    "Enter the app-specific password first." : {

    },
    "Every email in the first folder is filed and then moved to the second. With an iCloud alias, add a rule on icloud.com (Mail → Settings → Rules) that moves emails sent to the alias into %@. Paper Trail creates the second folder if needed, and never deletes email. While a device files an email, it sits in %@, so the Mac and iPhone never file the same one." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "Every email in the first folder is filed and then moved to the second. With an iCloud alias, add a rule on icloud.com (Mail → Settings → Rules) that moves emails sent to the alias into %1$@. Paper Trail creates the second folder if needed, and never deletes email. While a device files an email, it sits in %2$@, so the Mac and iPhone never file the same one."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Every week Paper Trail writes everything that isn't in the PDFs (amounts, VAT, paid bills, expense claims, learned rules) to Paper Trail/Export in iCloud Drive, as JSON and as a CSV for Excel or Numbers. The last 8 weeks are kept in Export/Backups. Import adds back documents and records that are missing from the index; it never changes or removes anything." : {

